.TH WELLBLOCK 1 "August 2026" "wellblock 1.1" "wellutils"
.SH NAME
Wellblock \- lists block devices (SATA/NVMe/MMC/virtio) with models, sizes, S.M.A.R.T. status
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wellblock
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIN\fR | \fIDEVICE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wellblock
.PP
Lists block devices (SATA/NVMe/MMC/virtio) with models, sizes,
serial numbers, SSD/HDD/removable classification, partitions with
filesystem and mount point, plus virtual devices such as zram and loop.
.PP
With an optional argument (a zero-based disk index or a device name such
as \fBsda\fR, \fBnvme0n1\fR or \fB/dev/sdb\fR) a detail view is printed for
that disk: model, serial, firmware, size, type, transport, partitions and
the S.M.A.R.T. status with a health verdict and the full attribute table
(requires \fBsmartmontools\fR; root/sudo needed for \fBsmartctl\fR).
.PP
When stdout is a terminal the output is drawn as a box; when piped a plain layout is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " ru|en|auto"
Force report language (default \fBauto\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-color " always|never|auto"
Force, disable, or auto-detect ANSI colour.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Plain text output without box drawing.
.TP
.B \-\-box
Force box drawing even when piped.
.TP
.B \-\-no-emoji
Disable emoji icons.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable JSON on stdout; errors still go to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose tracing.
.TP
.BI N | device
Disk detail view: a zero-based index from the summary order, or a device
name (\fBsda\fR, \fBnvme0n1\fR, \fB/dev/sdb\fR).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
.TP
.B 3
Requested disk not found, or runtime error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WELLUTILS_LANG
\fBru\fR or \fBen\fR; overrides locale detection.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables colour in auto mode.
.SH AUTHOR
wellbou_
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wellutils (1), .BR wellcpu (1), .BR wellgpu (1)
